# Binary Search Tree:

i) For every node, keys in left side are smaller and keys in right side are greater
ii) All keys are typically considered as distinct
iii) Like linked list, it is a linked data structure
iv) Implemented in C++ as map, set, multimap and multiset. and in Java as TreeSet and Treemap

# Time Complexity

| Operation        | Sorted Array | Unsorted Array | Linked List | Balanced BST | Hash Table |
| ---------------- | ------------ | -------------- | ----------- | ------------ | ---------- |
| Search           | O(log n)     | O(n)           | O(n)        | O(log n)     | O(1) avg   |
| Insert           | O(n)         | O(1)           | O(1)        | O(log n)     | O(1) avg   |
| Delete           | O(n)         | O(n)           | O(1)        | O(log n)     | O(1) avg   |
| Find Closest     | O(log n)     | O(n)           | O(n)        | O(log n)     | O(n)       |
| Sorted Traversal | O(n)         | O(n log n)     | O(n log n)  | O(n)         | O(n log n) |


